@startuml

salt
{
  <b>ORE STUDIO - REPORTING: RUN OUTPUTS</b>
  --
  <b>RUN: Group Consolidated Exposure - 4b7e1a02</b>
  --
  {#
    State | Completed | Took | Kind
    completed | 08:15:02 | 2 m 18 s | from report_instance_kind
  }
  --
  <b>WHAT THE SYSTEM SAID</b>
  --
  {
    Output message: Report execution completed.
  }
  --
  <b>THE ENGINE'S OUTPUT ARCHIVE</b>
  --
  {#
    Archive | reporting/runs/<instance-id>/output.tar.gz | [ Download ]
  }
  The archive is the run's output directory, archived by the compute run. This
  screen does not list the files inside it: no operation lists an archive's
  contents, so the reader opens the archive. An empty file list is not drawn.
  --
  <b>WHAT THE RUN SAID WAS WRONG</b>
  --
  {#
    Severity | Scope | Count
    error | Analytics | 8
    warning | Configuration | 3
  }
  11 rows in all. The archive is complete and the run still carries these. Open
  the errors for the subject of each one.
  --
  <b>THE ORE PACKAGE THIS RUN USED</b>
  --
  {#
    Pre-processing | Package | Action
    execute | prepared by ore.v1.ops.prepare_ore_package | [ Open package ]
    substitute | prepared_input_key from the definition | [ Open package ]
  }
  The package is the engine's input. It is what a person would run locally to
  reproduce the output. No read in the set returns it or lists its files.
  --
  <b>A RUN IN FLIGHT: NO OUTPUT YET</b>
  --
  {#
    State | Started | Output message | Archive
    running | 08:12:44 | - | not yet retrieved
  }
  The archive key is written only once the run's results are retrieved. The panel
  says the output will arrive; it does not show an empty archive.
  --
  <b>A RUN THAT FAILED: NOTHING TO TAKE</b>
  --
  {#
    State | Output message | Archive | Package
    failed | - | none | none
  }
  There is no archive and no package to hand over. The screen says so and sends
  the reader to the run's errors, including the Report scope rows the model
  states itself when no engine saw the failure.
}

@enduml
